#: ../../source/components_basic/17-component_touch.rst:105
msgid "Initialization in the ``setup()`` function. Here, we specify that the sensor pin will be used for input, the built-in LED will be used for output, and we start the serial communication to allow messages to be sent to the serial monitor."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/components_basic/17-component_touch.rst:115
msgid "Continuously, the Arduino checks if the touch sensor is activated. If touched, it turns on the LED and sends a \"Touch detected!\" message. If not touched, it turns off the LED and sends a \"No touch detected...\" message. A delay is introduced to prevent the sensor from being read too quickly."
msgstr ""

